This license covers the contents of `apps/apple/` — the Armada menu bar app. It
does NOT cover `docs/`, `design/` or `scripts/`, which are MIT licensed; see the
LICENSE file at the root of this repository.

WHY THIS IS NOT AN OPEN SOURCE LICENSE

Armada reads your transcripts. Every session it lists is a conversation you have
had with an agent — the code in it, the paths, the things you told it about your
work — across every account on the machine. It also spawns your own `claude` to
ask it questions, and opens terminals running agents on your behalf. Nobody
should grant that to software they cannot read, so the source stays readable,
auditable and buildable by anyone. What is sold, if and when a signed build is
distributed, is the notarized binary and the maintenance behind it — never
secrecy. This license is the narrowest set of terms that keeps both true.

